From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: neko-legends <neko-legends@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 09:06:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] deepseek_v41: four-Spark fixes from the TP=4 review (uneven
 slices, N ranks)

- candidates over the vocabulary: every rank sends k = min(count, widest
  slice) (pick.rank_top), narrower slices padded with (-inf, PAD) that sort
  after every real token; slots.cand_gather and engine.choose (the host
  merge drops the padding). Before: k = min(count, own width), so a count
  above 32,256 (nucleus rows ask for the whole vocabulary) all-gathered
  unequal sizes at TP=4
- draft head trim: per-rank lists from weights.block_bounds (was r * n:
  rank 2 refused to boot at TP=4); refuses rows wider than the narrowest
  slice by name
- TCP plan link: followers send a hello (magic, rank, world) and wait for
  rank 0's answer; rank 0 refuses strays, duplicates and another world
  size, orders the connections by rank, names a rank that never connected
- CLI: --tp above 2 only for families that declare it (CUDA_TP; deepseek_v41:
  (2, 4))
- attn_pf: BMQ 32 on a rank with 16 heads runs with 16 heads a program
  (was: a silent fallback to the chunk kernels)
- NVMe session tier: the world size is part of the compat ident
- speculative DSpark pass: skipped after windows of more than
  TF_DSV41_SPEC_MAX_COUNT (4,096) candidates a row; a sampled request with
  top_k ~32,000 hung every rank in the candidates' wait with it on (found
  while testing the above on four Sparks; the same requests pass without it)
- gate scorer: any rank count (was two); DSpark delta shards follow the
  128-block split
- tests: test_dsv41_four_sparks.py; the thread communicator refuses unequal
  all-gather sizes (NCCL's contract)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
